  "version": 1,
  "sectionId": "s3",
  "title": "A Residual Block Learns the Correction Around Identity",
  "introduction": "For one input feature vector $\\mathbf{x}$, let $\\mathcal{H}(\\mathbf{x})$ be the desired block output. Instead of fitting that mapping directly, the learned branch produces the correction $\\mathcal{F}(\\mathbf{x})=\\mathcal{H}(\\mathbf{x})-\\mathbf{x}$. An identity shortcut preserves the same $\\mathbf{x}$, and element-wise addition reconstructs $\\mathbf{y}=\\mathcal{F}(\\mathbf{x})+\\mathbf{x}$.",
