      "explanation": "Element-wise addition changes the available result from the separate terms $\\mathbf{x}$ and $\\mathcal{F}(\\mathbf{x})$ to the output $\\mathbf{y}=\\mathcal{F}(\\mathbf{x})+\\mathbf{x}$. When the learned correction equals $\\mathcal{H}(\\mathbf{x})-\\mathbf{x}$, this output equals the desired $\\mathcal{H}(\\mathbf{x})$. If identity is desired, the branch only needs to approach zero.",
