  "takeaway": "The invariant is that the shortcut preserves the same $\\mathbf{x}$ while the learned branch supplies only its correction: if $\\mathcal{F}(\\mathbf{x})=\\mathcal{H}(\\mathbf{x})-\\mathbf{x}$, then $\\mathbf{y}=\\mathcal{F}(\\mathbf{x})+\\mathbf{x}=\\mathcal{H}(\\mathbf{x})$.",
